WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:07.080
Welcome to the course Conversational AI Concepts, Capabilities, and Use Cases.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:14.720
Think about the last time you interacted with a chat bot at work or as a customer.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:19.551
Maybe it answered a simple question right away,

00:00:19.551 --> 00:00:26.152
or maybe it sent you through a few fixed options and left you feeling stuck when

00:00:26.152 --> 00:00:28.760
your question did not quite fit.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.440
That difference in experience is not accidental.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.581
It comes down to how the conversational system is designed,

00:00:38.581 --> 00:00:43.640
what it is capable of understanding, and how it is implemented.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:51.237
It's This course focuses on helping you understand those differences so you can

00:00:51.237 --> 00:00:57.917
evaluate Conversational AI solutions with clarity and make better decisions in a

00:00:57.917 --> 00:00:59.320
business context.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:04.327
By the end of this course, you will be able to explain what

00:01:04.327 --> 00:01:10.601
conversational AI is and how it differs from traditional automation systems such

00:01:10.601 --> 00:01:13.079
as IVR and rule based chat bots.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:19.460
Describe how conversational AI works, including the key technologies that

00:01:19.460 --> 00:01:25.083
enable it to understand input, interpret intent, and generate responses,

00:01:25.083 --> 00:01:29.935
and differentiate between traditional chat bots, AI chat bots,

00:01:29.935 --> 00:01:34.942
and agentic AI chat bots, and evaluate implementation approaches

00:01:34.942 --> 00:01:38.640
based on organizational needs and capabilities.